      en: "Val-de-Travers is a valley in the canton of Neuchâtel, Switzerland, stretching 25 km from Noiraigue to the French border. It is famous for absinthe production; the region is the birthplace of the green spirit. The Areuse Gorge features deep limestone cliffs. The river Areuse flows through the valley into Lake Neuchâtel. The Creux du Van rock cirque is at its head. Part of the UNESCO Jura Biosphere Reserve, the economy relies on tourism, watchmaking, and agriculture. Major towns include Couvet, Fleurier, and Môtiers. The valley has around 12,000 inhabitants.",
