      en: "Val Bavona is a rugged valley in the Swiss canton of Ticino, known for its wild nature and numerous waterfalls. Stretching 15 km from Cavergno to the Cristallina glacier, the valley floor lies at about 400 m above sea level, while surrounding peaks exceed 2500 m. Traditional stone houses, called rustici, dot the landscape, along with old bridges and mills. The valley is part of the UNESCO World Heritage site Monte San Giorgio. The Foroglio waterfall, with a drop of 100 m, is a major attraction. Geologically, the valley consists mainly of gneiss and granite. Agriculture focuses on cattle breeding, but tourism has become the main economic driver. The area is rich in rare flora and fauna, including the golden eagle and alpine ibex.",
